From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:07:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] combase, ole32: Release marshal data of a disconnected object
 quietly, and drop its running object table entry.

Word disconnects its objects at exit and then revokes their running
object table entries and global interface table cookies: the marshal
data then has no stub manager, CoReleaseMarshalData failed with
RPC_E_INVALID_OBJREF after two ERRs.  Windows 11 answers S_OK for data
of an object that was disconnected, of an apartment that has gone and
for table data released already.  Its running object table takes such
a registration for gone: IsRunning answers S_FALSE, GetObject and
GetTimeOfLastChange MK_E_UNAVAILABLE, EnumRunning leaves it out, and
only Revoke still knows its cookie (tools/startupgapsprobe comrel).
ole32 asks combase whether the object of an entry made in this process
is still connected, without unmarshaling it, and retires the ones that
are not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

